# CODEFLOW ignore file
# --------------------
# Excludes non-production paths from external code-scanning (CODEFLOW and
# similar regex/heuristic scanners) so their findings reflect the runtime app
# surface, not documentation content, generated data, dev tooling, or the
# security analyzer's own intentional test fixtures.
#
# NOTE: This file only takes effect if the scanning product supports a
# `.codeflowignore` (or equivalent path-exclusion) config AND scans an
# authenticated checkout of the latest `main`. See
# docs/enterprise/CODEFLOW_VS_INTERNAL_HEALTH.md for how to re-auth + rescan and
# for the full accepted-risk rationale behind the remaining production findings.
#
# We deliberately DO NOT exclude application source under src/app, src/components,
# or src/lib — real code stays in scope. Only non-runtime artifacts are ignored.

# --- Dependencies / build output ---
node_modules/
.next/
coverage/
.tmp/
out/

# --- Vendored documentation content (data, not executable app code) ---
# ~527 JSON files ingested from the Cyware Theneo export. May contain example
# curl/JS/Python/VBA snippets (e.g. Shell(), os.system, eval) that are docs, not
# app behaviour.
src/content/**
**/*.md

# --- Unit / e2e tests, including the security analyzer's own detector fixtures ---
# These files intentionally contain sample sink call-sites (eval, Function,
# spawn, dangerouslySetInnerHTML) as *strings* fed to the detectors under test.
# They are never shipped or reachable at runtime.
**/__tests__/**
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
e2e/

# --- Dev / CI / build tooling (trusted, not on the web request path) ---
# Includes the code-health analyzer (scripts/health/**), ingest/build scripts,
# and secret scanners that legitimately use child_process for local automation.
scripts/

# --- Generated analyzer ledger (data, not code) ---
scripts/health/findings.json
scripts/health/score.json
